  <p class="note">
    skyBlip Bravo, a Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1, carries no ADS-L radio
    under skyBlip firmware: it receives ADS-B on 1090&nbsp;MHz and transmits
    nothing, so no ADS-L declaration covers it. Its CE document is Seeed&rsquo;s
    <a href="https://files.seeedstudio.com/Seeed_Certificate/documents_certificate/100093876-CE.pdf">verification of compliance LGT26F105C01</a>,
    issued by Shenzhen LGT Test Service on 8 Sep 2026 under the Radio Equipment
    Directive.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">The address</h2>
  <h3>Manufacturer page 49, AMT entry 58, prefix 0, assigned on 5 October 2026.</h3>

  <p>
    The declaration states that the product uses an approved address range
    (F.2.2). skyBlip applied to the ADS-L registry on 20 September 2026, and
    FLARM assigned manufacturer page 49, AMT entry 58, with manufacturer prefix
    0, under ticket #228794. Each unit gets its 16 bits below the prefix at
    activation: skyblip.eu assigns the serial against the unit&rsquo;s chip id
    and signs it, and a unit that holds no serial neither transmits nor
    receives. The application, the log of the exchange and the reasons behind
    it are on <%= link_to_page "ads-l-registry", label: "the ADS-L registry page" %>.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">The declaration</h2>
  <h3 id="declaration">The appendix template, filled in for skyBlip Go and Go+.</h3>

  <p>
    In accordance with ED Decision 2022/024/R and the attached Technical
    Specification for ADS-L transmissions using the SRD-860 frequency band
    (&ldquo;ADS-L 4 SRD 860&rdquo;).
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Manufacturer</th><td>FRANCOIS CATUHE EI, 23 cours de Verdun, 33000 Bordeaux, France</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Product name</th><td>skyBlip Go, on a LilyGO T-Echo. skyBlip Go+, on a LilyGO T-Echo Plus, is the same product with accessories.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Device P/N</th><td>skyBlipGo</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Firmware version</th><td>skyBlip 1.0.0</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Standard</th><td>ADS-L 4 SRD860 Issue 2</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Transmission parameters</h3>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th>Transmission bands and power levels</th>
          <td>M-band only, 868.2 and 868.4&nbsp;MHz, alternating by UTC second. The firmware caps the output at +14&nbsp;dBm e.r.p., computed from the antenna&rsquo;s datasheet gain and not yet measured. The appendix asks for 12 to 14&nbsp;dBm e.r.p. on M-band. Nothing is transmitted on the O-band.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Optional parameters transmitted</th>
          <td>none. The Traffic payload carries every field of G.1, and no secure signature (E.4) is appended.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Receive capabilities</th>
          <td>M-band 868.2 and 868.4&nbsp;MHz, 400&nbsp;ms on each channel every second. O-band HDR 869.525&nbsp;MHz, 190&nbsp;ms every second, for the Traffic Uplink. O-band LDR is not received.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>What the manufacturer additionally declares</h3>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Statement</th><th>Holds</th><th>Why</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th>Robust design processes and production controls ensure consistent quality and compliance</th>
          <td>to write</td>
          <td>LilyGO builds the hardware. skyBlip builds the firmware, and every build runs the conformance suite in <a href="https://github.com/fcatuhe/skyblip/tree/main/firmware/test/adsl"><code>firmware/test/adsl/</code></a>, one case per clause of Issue 2. The statement still has to say how both halves are controlled.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>The product meets all relevant EU requirements, is CE marked and documented</th>
          <td>Go only</td>
          <td>the T-Echo has LilyGO&rsquo;s RED attestation. The T-Echo Plus has no published CE document.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>The product uses an approved address range (F.2.2)</th>
          <td>yes</td>
          <td>AMT entry 58, manufacturer page 49, prefix 0, assigned by the registry.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>The product nominally transmits at least the Traffic and Status payloads (Subpart G)</th>
          <td>no</td>
          <td>Traffic is transmitted, at 1&nbsp;Hz airborne and 0.1&nbsp;Hz on the ground. The Status payload (G.2) is not transmitted yet.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

